<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλ-ίνης</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλῖνος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφις, ὁ,</span> a
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blind</i> snake, perh.
				<i>Pseudopus pallasi,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλίναι ὄφεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					567b25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίνοις ὄφεσιν</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				604b25
			</span></i>: called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλώψ</span></b>  in
				<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				492
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				8.13
			</span></i> (on the accent, v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.66
			</span></i>); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλίας</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλών</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (unless these are errors for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλίνας, τυφλώψ</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλιης</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τυφλίς,</span> and
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφαις</span>
			=
			<i>caeciola, caecilia, ciccola,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i> (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλίνης,
				τυφλίας</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; τυφλείας</span>
			=
			<i>caecula,</i> ib.:—cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωφίας.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλῖνος, ὁ,</span> a Nile fish, <i><span class="en">
				Marc.Sid.
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλίνης </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλῆνις, τυφλενες</span> codd.) <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				4.56
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύφλην</span> (nom.) <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.312b
			</span></i>: 
				Dim.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλινίδιον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				Xenocr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				2.58.152
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φλην</span>-codd.).</div>
